<h1 data-eusoft-scrollable-element=3D"1">Instructions</h1>
<h2>Setting Up Your Development Environment</h2>
<p>See the <a href=3D"https://15445.courses.cs.cmu.edu/fall2021/project0/#i=
nstructions">Project #0 instructions</a> on how to create your private repo=
sitory and setup your development environment.</p>
<p class=3D"warning bg-info">
    <i class=3D"trigger fa fa-exclamation-triangle fa-lg" data-eusoft-scrol=
lable-element=3D"1"></i>
    You must pull the latest changes from the upstream BusTub repository fo=
r test files and other supplementary files we provide in this project.
</p>

<h2>Testing</h2>
<p>You can test the individual components of this assigment using our testi=
ng framework. We use <a href=3D"https://github.com/google/googletest">GTest=
</a> for unit test cases. We provide you with a single unit test file, <cod=
e>test/execution/executor_test</code>, that implements tests for basic func=
tionality of some executors.</p>
<pre>cd build
make executor_test
./test/executor_test
</pre>

<p>As you progress through the project, you can enable individual tests in =
<code>executor_test</code> by removing the <code>DISABLED_</code> prefix fr=
om the test case names.</p>
<h2>Memory safety</h2>
<p>To ensure your implementation does not contain memory leaks, you can run=
 the test with <a href=3D"http://valgrind.org/">Valgrind</a>.</p>
<pre>cd build
make executor_test
valgrind --trace-children=3Dyes \
   --leak-check=3Dfull \
   --track-origins=3Dyes \
   --soname-synonyms=3Dsomalloc=3D*jemalloc* \
   --error-exitcode=3D1 \
   --suppressions=3D../build_support/valgrind.supp \
